    given-names: Diogo
version: 0.2.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DiogoRibeiro7/article-reminders"
url: "https://github.com/DiogoRibeiro7/article-reminders"
abstract: >-
  A research workflow application for the operational side of writing papers:
  which paper needs attention, why, and what the next concrete piece of work is.
  It tracks the lifecycle of manuscripts from idea to publication, keeps its data
  in plain files that remain readable without it, and uses GitHub commit activity
  as evidence rather than as a database - which lets it answer the one question a
  task list cannot: the analysis is moving, but is the manuscript?
keywords:
  - research workflow
  - academic writing
  - manuscript tracking
  - reminders
  - research software
